<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sari, Iran</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sari is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mazandaran">Mazandaran</a> province in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, on the plain between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alborz">Alborz</a> mountains and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a>. It was a seat of the Dabuyid ispahbads of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabaristan">Tabaristan</a> and later of local dynasties such as the Bavandids and the Marashis. It remains an important agricultural and commercial centre of the Caspian lowlands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sari-iran.jpg" alt="Sari, Iran" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: matin fattahi · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D9%85%DB%8C%D8%AF%D8%A7%D9%86_%D8%B3%D8%A7%D8%B9%D8%AA_%D8%B3%D8%A7%D8%B1%DB%8C_-_panoramio_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
